More than just a Set Interpreter

The Set and the Range class have a different relationship to the formal theory of set theory than the standard collection classes (List and (key,value) Map) and (key,value) Set have to ZF set theory. The Set class is a set from the formal theory of set theory and has its own API. But the Range class has some self-contained operations beyond the normal set theory operations and is a kind of intermediate between what we see in the standard collection classes and what we see in Set. In other words, it's more advanced than just an API that follows the self-description of the standard collection classes.

Range class - Oracle developer documentation

Out of the box, the same ol' JDK-internal Range has been exposed:

// Range in Java 14

