Range<BigDecimal> r = Range.of(BigDecimal.valueOf(1.0), BigDecimal.valueOf(100.0));

// convert to a Range of integers to show how it works
Range<Integer> rng = r.as(range(Integer.class));
for (Integer n : rng) {
System.out.println(n);
}
}


But Javadoc states that the class exists in JDK only, and it's definitely different from other ranges that are part of ORACLE JDK14.

The main point is that without additional information, it's hard to figure out how the new range class interacts with other ranges. I'd like to make it easier for us to stay up to date with the development of the JDK. Plus, I like interfaces and have already used several of them for my projects in the past, and had a chance to participate in working on an interface for the project I'm currently working on.
