## Step 7: Play around

Solve other problems using LaTeX.

For example, determine the 10,000th digit in the decimal expansion of $\frac{45}{2} + 11 \sqrt{3}.$ Note that your answer is not surprising, since this approximation using scratch paper would require an infinite amount of paper, and is computationally infeasible, hence in the first place, it is impossible.

Or determine the current generation of YINs - Young Intellectuals (Cantonese name 粹英), in terms of number of people at this time of writing. (An older generation of this group, called YAP - Young Appreciators, were concentrated in the middle of the 1980s.)

Or determine the probability that $\sqrt{55 - 15 \sqrt{3}}$ and $\sqrt{55 + 15 \sqrt{3}}$ both lie inside the unit circle.

