## PHP offers reliable error handling

The PHP community is very good at monitoring websites that cannot handle error conditions gracefully (e.g. fault injection). This is very important because PHP is so easy to write that it is all too easy to accidentally write a program that will crash with an error when a case no-one thought about comes up. PHP offers reliable handling of errors and it is easy to turn on.

The default behavior of PHP is to only output an error to STDERR. (Display this if you want to see what the error says.) To handle errors in a different way use the error_reporting() function:

<?
echo error_reporting(E_ALL);
$err= error_reporting(); // This is the error_reporting() error

